    "# Closed Hi-Hat Sound\n",
    "As seen in previous sections so does the closed hi-hat start it's life by defining a discrete time vector *t*, and creating an array of pseudo random values in an array of same length as *t*. then an envelope is applied to the final output as described in the *Kick Sound* section."
