    "# High-Pass Filter\n",
    "A high-pass filter removes low frequency components from a signal preserving the higher frequencies.\n",
    "In drum synthesis, high-pass filters are useful for shaping sound of high frequency drums like snares, hi-hat, crashes, rides and splashes and hats in general. The filter removes unwanted low-frequency energy, making the sound sharper and clearer. This filter truly shows it's power in the making of the final instrument the open hi-hat which will be explained in the following section.\n",
    "\n",
    "The high-pass filter implemented in this project is a first-order high-pass filter. Mathematically it looks like this: $$ y[n] = \\alpha \\cdot (y[n-1]+x[n]-x[n-1]) $$\n",
    "where:\n",
    "$x[n]$ = input signal\n",
    "$y[n]$ = filtered output\n",
    "$\\alpha$ = smoothing parameter - *controls cutoff behavior*\n",
    "\n",
    "The term $x[n]-x[n-1]$ captures rapid changes in the signal, allowing high-frequencies to pass through while attenuating slower variations corresponding to low frequencies. The parameter $\\alpha$ determines how strongly the filter affects the input signal, with values close to 1 preserving most of the original signal. In this project this implementation of a high-pass filter is only used on the open hi-hat, but the reason as to why will be explained in the following section."
   ],
   "id": "7ba50152dd41f1dc"
  },
  {
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-04-14T09:50:46.166895Z",
